export function DocsArticle() {
  return (
<article className="max-w-[760px] min-w-0 pb-24"><h2 id="abstract" className="group mt-16 scroll-mt-24 border-t border-line pt-10 text-[26px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] first:mt-0 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><a href="#abstract" className="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline gap-3"><span className="mono text-[12px] font-normal text-ink-faint">01</span><span>Abstract</span><span className="mono text-[14px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h2><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">A token&#x27;s identity on Solana lives in its Metaplex metadata account: a name, a symbol, and a URI pointing at an image and description. Almost every launch freezes that account the moment it is created. STS-1 does the opposite. It specifies tokens that are born shiftable, the three ways a shift can be requested, the single transaction that performs it, and the guarantees that hold across every rewrite.</p><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">The result is a token that can tell a story over time. It can be one thing at launch and another at graduation, change on a creator&#x27;s command, or continuously become whatever the market is watching. Holders never move, never migrate, never claim. The token they hold simply becomes something new.</p><h2 id="motivation" className="group mt-16 scroll-mt-24 border-t border-line pt-10 text-[26px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] first:mt-0 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><a href="#motivation" className="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline gap-3"><span className="mono text-[12px] font-normal text-ink-faint">02</span><span>Motivation</span><span className="mono text-[14px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h2><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">Memecoins are narratives, and narratives move faster than a fixed ticker. Today a project that wants a new identity has two options: launch a new token and ask everyone to move, or live with the old one. Both lose. Liquidity fragments, holders are left behind, and the history that made the token valuable is gone.</p><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">Solana&#x27;s metadata program already supports rewriting a token&#x27;s identity. What was missing is a standard: who may do it, when, how it is authorized, what it may never touch, and how anyone watching can follow along. STS-1 is that standard.</p><h2 id="terminology" className="group mt-16 scroll-mt-24 border-t border-line pt-10 text-[26px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] first:mt-0 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><a href="#terminology" className="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline gap-3"><span className="mono text-[12px] font-normal text-ink-faint">03</span><span>Terminology</span><span className="mono text-[14px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h2><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">The key words <span className="mono text-[12px] font-semibold tracking-[0.06em] text-ink">MUST</span>, <span className="mono text-[12px] font-semibold tracking-[0.06em] text-ink">MUST NOT</span>, <span className="mono text-[12px] font-semibold tracking-[0.06em] text-ink">SHOULD</span> and <span className="mono text-[12px] font-semibold tracking-[0.06em] text-ink">MAY</span> are to be read as described in RFC 2119.</p><div className="no-scrollbar mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line"><table className="w-full min-w-[560px] border-collapse text-left text-[13px]"><thead><tr className="border-b border-line bg-card"><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">Term</th><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Shiftable token</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">An SPL token launched under STS-1, whose metadata account is shiftable and controlled by the launchpad.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Identity</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">The triple of name, symbol and URI in the metadata account, and the image and description the URI resolves to.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Shift</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">One transaction that replaces a token&#x27;s identity with a new one. Nothing else about the token changes.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Generation</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">How many shifts a token has undergone. Zero at launch, plus one per shift.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Update authority</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">The key permitted by the Token Metadata program to rewrite the metadata account. Under STS-1, the launchpad.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Mode</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">The policy that decides when a token shifts: manual, scheduled, or auto.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Keeper</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">The launchpad&#x27;s service that applies scheduled and auto shifts.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Lease</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">A short lock that guarantees one shift at a time per token.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="token" className="group mt-16 scroll-mt-24 border-t border-line pt-10 text-[26px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] first:mt-0 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><a href="#token" className="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline gap-3"><span className="mono text-[12px] font-normal text-ink-faint">04</span><span>The shiftable token</span><span className="mono text-[14px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h2><h3 id="token-mint" className="group mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]"><a href="#token-mint" className="cursor-pointer">Mint and supply<span className="mono ml-2 text-[12px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h3><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">A shiftable token is a classic SPL Token mint with <code className="mono rounded border border-line bg-card-2 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[12.5px] text-ink">6</code> decimals and a fixed supply of <code className="mono rounded border border-line bg-card-2 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[12.5px] text-ink">1,000,000,000</code>. The mint authority is revoked at creation; the supply can never change. The mint address is the token&#x27;s permanent identifier and <span className="mono text-[12px] font-semibold tracking-[0.06em] text-ink">MUST</span> remain the same for the token&#x27;s entire life.</p><h3 id="token-metadata" className="group mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]"><a href="#token-metadata" className="cursor-pointer">Metadata account<span className="mono ml-2 text-[12px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h3><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">The token&#x27;s Metaplex metadata account <span className="mono text-[12px] font-semibold tracking-[0.06em] text-ink">MUST</span> be created with <code className="mono rounded border border-line bg-card-2 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[12.5px] text-ink">is_mutable = true</code>, and its update authority <span className="mono text-[12px] font-semibold tracking-[0.06em] text-ink">MUST</span> be the launchpad&#x27;s key. This is set by the launchpad&#x27;s Meteora Dynamic Bonding Curve configuration (<code className="mono rounded border border-line bg-card-2 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[12.5px] text-ink">tokenUpdateAuthority = PartnerUpdateAuthority</code>), so every token created from it inherits the same authority, without exception.</p><div className="mt-5 rounded-xl border px-4 py-3 border-line-strong bg-card"><div className="mono text-[10.5px] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-ink-faint">Invariant</div><div className="mt-1 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">The launchpad never transfers the update authority and never sets <code className="mono rounded border border-line bg-card-2 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[12.5px] text-ink">is_mutable</code> to false. A token whose metadata is found immutable, or whose authority is not the launchpad, is marked <em>dormant</em> and is never shifted.</div></div><h3 id="token-identity" className="group mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]"><a href="#token-identity" className="cursor-pointer">Identity<span className="mono ml-2 text-[12px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h3><div className="no-scrollbar mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line"><table className="w-full min-w-[560px] border-collapse text-left text-[13px]"><thead><tr className="border-b border-line bg-card"><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">Field</th><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">Rule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">name</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">1 to 32 characters.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">symbol</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">1 to 10 letters or digits. Case is preserved.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">uri</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">An IPFS document (https://ipfs.io/ipfs/…), at most 200 bytes, pinned by the launchpad.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">image</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">PNG, JPEG, WEBP or GIF, up to 5 MB, pinned to IPFS. A shift without an image keeps the current one.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">description</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Optional, up to 500 characters.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 id="token-json" className="group mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]"><a href="#token-json" className="cursor-pointer">Off-chain document<span className="mono ml-2 text-[12px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h3><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">Each identity points at a JSON document in the format wallets already read. STS-1 adds two attributes, so the token&#x27;s shiftable nature is visible to any marketplace or explorer that shows traits.</p><div className="term mt-4"><div className="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-line px-3 py-1.5"><span className="mono text-[11px] text-ink-faint">metadata.json</span><button type="button" className="mono cursor-pointer rounded px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[11px] text-ink-faint transition-colors hover:bg-card-2 hover:text-ink">copy</button></div><pre className="no-scrollbar overflow-x-auto p-3 text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed"><code className="mono text-ink-soft">{`{
  "name": "Shapeshifter",
  "symbol": "Shift",
  "image": "https://ipfs.io/ipfs/bafy…",
  "description": "What it is, and what it might become.",
  "showName": true,
  "createdOn": "https://shift-spl.com",
  "twitter": "https://x.com/…",
  "website": "https://…",
  "attributes": [
    { "trait_type": "Shifts", "value": 3 },
    { "trait_type": "Mode", "value": "scheduled" }
  ]
}`}</code></pre></div><h2 id="shift" className="group mt-16 scroll-mt-24 border-t border-line pt-10 text-[26px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] first:mt-0 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><a href="#shift" className="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline gap-3"><span className="mono text-[12px] font-normal text-ink-faint">05</span><span>Shifts</span><span className="mono text-[14px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h2><h3 id="shift-tx" className="group mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]"><a href="#shift-tx" className="cursor-pointer">The transaction<span className="mono ml-2 text-[12px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h3><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">A shift is a single Solana transaction, signed and paid for by the update authority, containing exactly two instructions: the metadata rewrite and a memo that marks it.</p><div className="term mt-4"><div className="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-line px-3 py-1.5"><span className="mono text-[11px] text-ink-faint">shift transaction</span><button type="button" className="mono cursor-pointer rounded px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[11px] text-ink-faint transition-colors hover:bg-card-2 hover:text-ink">copy</button></div><pre className="no-scrollbar overflow-x-auto p-3 text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed"><code className="mono text-ink-soft">{`UpdateMetadataAccountV2  (Token Metadata, discriminator 15)
  accounts
    [w]  metadata          PDA("metadata", METAPLEX, mint)
    [s]  update_authority  the launchpad
  data
    Some(DataV2 {
      name, symbol, uri            ← the new identity
      seller_fee_basis_points      ← carried over
      creators, collection, uses   ← carried over
    })
    update_authority       None    ← unchanged
    primary_sale_happened  None    ← unchanged
    is_mutable             None    ← unchanged

Memo  "shift:shift:\u003cgeneration\u003e"`}</code></pre></div><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">Before the transaction is built, the new image (if any) and the new metadata document are pinned to IPFS. Every field the rewrite does not intend to change is read from the current account and written back unchanged.</p><h3 id="shift-invariants" className="group mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]"><a href="#shift-invariants" className="cursor-pointer">Invariants<span className="mono ml-2 text-[12px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h3><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">A shift <span className="mono text-[12px] font-semibold tracking-[0.06em] text-ink">MUST NOT</span> change any of the following. They hold across every generation:</p><div className="no-scrollbar mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line"><table className="w-full min-w-[560px] border-collapse text-left text-[13px]"><thead><tr className="border-b border-line bg-card"><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">Never changes</th><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">Why it matters</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Mint address</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Every wallet, pool, chart and integration keeps pointing at the same token.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Supply and decimals</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">No dilution, ever. The mint authority is gone.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Balances and token accounts</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Holders do nothing. There is nothing to migrate or claim.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Liquidity pool</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">The bonding curve, and after graduation the DAMM v2 pool, keep trading the same mint.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Update authority, mutability</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">The rules can&#x27;t be quietly changed mid-life.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Royalties, creators, collection</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Carried over byte for byte.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 id="shift-generations" className="group mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]"><a href="#shift-generations" className="cursor-pointer">Generations<span className="mono ml-2 text-[12px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h3><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">Each shift increments the token&#x27;s generation by exactly one and is recorded with its previous identity, its new identity, what caused it, and the transaction signature. The history is append-only and public on every token page and through the API.</p><h2 id="modes" className="group mt-16 scroll-mt-24 border-t border-line pt-10 text-[26px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] first:mt-0 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><a href="#modes" className="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline gap-3"><span className="mono text-[12px] font-normal text-ink-faint">06</span><span>Shift modes</span><span className="mono text-[14px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h2><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">Every token declares a mode at launch. The mode answers one question: <em>who decides when this token becomes something else?</em></p><div className="no-scrollbar mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line"><table className="w-full min-w-[560px] border-collapse text-left text-[13px]"><thead><tr className="border-b border-line bg-card"><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">Mode</th><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">Who decides</th><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">When</th><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">Changeable</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">manual</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">The creator</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Whenever they sign a request</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Can switch to auto</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">scheduled</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">The creator, in advance</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">At fixed times after launch</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">No: the plan is fixed</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">auto</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">The market</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Every keeper interval</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Can switch to manual</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 id="mode-manual" className="group mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]"><a href="#mode-manual" className="cursor-pointer">Manual<span className="mono ml-2 text-[12px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h3><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">The creator rewrites the token from its page. They choose a new name, ticker and optionally an image, and sign a message with the wallet that launched it. Signing is free; the launchpad pays for and submits the transaction. Only the launch wallet can request a manual shift, and every request expires after five minutes.</p><h3 id="mode-scheduled" className="group mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]"><a href="#mode-scheduled" className="cursor-pointer">Scheduled<span className="mono ml-2 text-[12px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h3><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">The creator commits the token&#x27;s future at launch: up to 4 identities, each with a time in hours after launch. Times <span className="mono text-[12px] font-semibold tracking-[0.06em] text-ink">MUST</span> strictly increase and fall within 720 hours (30 days). An entry without an image inherits the previous one.</p><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">Future identities are hidden. The API reveals only when each lands, never what it will be, until it is applied. A scheduled token cannot be shifted manually and its plan cannot be edited: what was committed at launch is what happens.</p><h3 id="mode-auto" className="group mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]"><a href="#mode-auto" className="cursor-pointer">Auto · trending<span className="mono ml-2 text-[12px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h3><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">The token follows the market. On every keeper run it becomes a memecoin trending on Solana at that moment, taking that coin&#x27;s name, ticker and image. Trending data comes from Birdeye&#x27;s trending list, falling back to DexScreener&#x27;s most-boosted Solana tokens when Birdeye is unavailable. The image is copied to IPFS so the token never depends on another project&#x27;s servers.</p><div className="mt-5 rounded-xl border px-4 py-3 border-line-strong bg-card"><div className="mono text-[10.5px] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-ink-faint">Note</div><div className="mt-1 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">An auto token borrows an identity, not a token. It never holds, trades or links to the coin it mirrors.</div></div><h2 id="authorization" className="group mt-16 scroll-mt-24 border-t border-line pt-10 text-[26px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] first:mt-0 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><a href="#authorization" className="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline gap-3"><span className="mono text-[12px] font-normal text-ink-faint">07</span><span>Creator authorization</span><span className="mono text-[14px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h2><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">Creator actions are authorized by an Ed25519 signature over a plain-text message, not by a transaction. The wallet proves it holds the launch key; the launchpad&#x27;s update authority performs the write. The message is human-readable in the wallet prompt and names the exact change.</p><div className="term mt-4"><div className="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-line px-3 py-1.5"><span className="mono text-[11px] text-ink-faint">shift request</span><button type="button" className="mono cursor-pointer rounded px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[11px] text-ink-faint transition-colors hover:bg-card-2 hover:text-ink">copy</button></div><pre className="no-scrollbar overflow-x-auto p-3 text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed"><code className="mono text-ink-soft">{`Shift: shift my token
token: ShFt4k…9sV1
name: Shapeshifter
symbol: Shift
image: https://ipfs.io/ipfs/bafy…
issued: 1792540800000`}</code></pre></div><div className="term mt-4"><div className="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-line px-3 py-1.5"><span className="mono text-[11px] text-ink-faint">mode request</span><button type="button" className="mono cursor-pointer rounded px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[11px] text-ink-faint transition-colors hover:bg-card-2 hover:text-ink">copy</button></div><pre className="no-scrollbar overflow-x-auto p-3 text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed"><code className="mono text-ink-soft">{`Shift: change shift mode
token: ShFt4k…9sV1
mode: auto
issued: 1792540800000`}</code></pre></div><ol className="mt-5 space-y-0"><li className="relative flex gap-4 pb-5 last:pb-0"><span className="absolute top-7 bottom-0 left-[13px] w-px bg-line"></span><span className="mono flex size-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-line-strong bg-card text-[11px] text-ink">1</span><div className="pt-0.5"><div className="text-[14px] font-semibold">Rebuild</div><div className="mt-0.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">The server rebuilds the message from the request body. Any difference in token, values or time invalidates it.</div></div></li><li className="relative flex gap-4 pb-5 last:pb-0"><span className="absolute top-7 bottom-0 left-[13px] w-px bg-line"></span><span className="mono flex size-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-line-strong bg-card text-[11px] text-ink">2</span><div className="pt-0.5"><div className="text-[14px] font-semibold">Freshness</div><div className="mt-0.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">The <code className="mono rounded border border-line bg-card-2 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[12.5px] text-ink">issued</code> timestamp <span className="mono text-[12px] font-semibold tracking-[0.06em] text-ink">MUST</span> be within five minutes of the server clock, so a signature can&#x27;t be saved and replayed later.</div></div></li><li className="relative flex gap-4 pb-5 last:pb-0"><span className="absolute top-7 bottom-0 left-[13px] w-px bg-line"></span><span className="mono flex size-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-line-strong bg-card text-[11px] text-ink">3</span><div className="pt-0.5"><div className="text-[14px] font-semibold">Signer</div><div className="mt-0.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">The signature MUST verify against the token&#x27;s creator: the wallet that paid for its launch.</div></div></li><li className="relative flex gap-4 pb-5 last:pb-0"><span className="mono flex size-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-line-strong bg-card text-[11px] text-ink">4</span><div className="pt-0.5"><div className="text-[14px] font-semibold">Execute</div><div className="mt-0.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Only then is the shift leased, pinned, signed by the update authority and broadcast.</div></div></li></ol><h2 id="keeper" className="group mt-16 scroll-mt-24 border-t border-line pt-10 text-[26px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] first:mt-0 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><a href="#keeper" className="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline gap-3"><span className="mono text-[12px] font-normal text-ink-faint">08</span><span>The keeper</span><span className="mono text-[14px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h2><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">The keeper is the process that shifts tokens without anyone asking. It runs two loops: every 30 seconds it applies any scheduled identity that has come due, and on a fixed interval (<code className="mono rounded border border-line bg-card-2 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[12.5px] text-ink">KEEPER_INTERVAL_MIN</code>, 30 minutes by default, one setting for the whole platform) it rewrites every auto-mode token.</p><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">Auto tokens are dealt different coins so the platform never turns into twenty copies of the same thing, and the deal rotates each round. A token is never handed the coin it already mirrors.</p><div className="term mt-4"><div className="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-line px-3 py-1.5"><span className="mono text-[11px] text-ink-faint">assignment</span><button type="button" className="mono cursor-pointer rounded px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[11px] text-ink-faint transition-colors hover:bg-card-2 hover:text-ink">copy</button></div><pre className="no-scrollbar overflow-x-auto p-3 text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed"><code className="mono text-ink-soft">{`round = floor(now / interval)
for token[i] in auto tokens (oldest first):
  pick = trending[(i + round) mod n]
  while pick.mint == token.mirror_mint or pick.symbol == token.symbol:
    pick = next in trending
  shift(token, pick)`}</code></pre></div><h2 id="concurrency" className="group mt-16 scroll-mt-24 border-t border-line pt-10 text-[26px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] first:mt-0 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><a href="#concurrency" className="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline gap-3"><span className="mono text-[12px] font-normal text-ink-faint">09</span><span>Concurrency and safety</span><span className="mono text-[14px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h2><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">Creators, schedules and the keeper all shift through one code path. Before any work begins it takes a lease: a conditional write that succeeds only if the token is still at the expected generation and no other shift holds it. Leases expire after three minutes, so a crashed process can never wedge a token.</p><div className="no-scrollbar mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line"><table className="w-full min-w-[560px] border-collapse text-left text-[13px]"><thead><tr className="border-b border-line bg-card"><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">Situation</th><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">Outcome</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Two requests for the same token at once</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">One wins the lease; the other is told a shift is in progress.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Transaction fails on-chain</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">The lease is released; nothing is recorded; the token keeps its identity.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Metadata found immutable or not ours</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">The token is marked dormant and skipped forever after.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Trending sources unavailable</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">The keeper skips the round. Tokens keep their current identity.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="lifecycle" className="group mt-16 scroll-mt-24 border-t border-line pt-10 text-[26px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] first:mt-0 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><a href="#lifecycle" className="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline gap-3"><span className="mono text-[12px] font-normal text-ink-faint">10</span><span>Launch lifecycle</span><span className="mono text-[14px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h2><ol className="mt-5 space-y-0"><li className="relative flex gap-4 pb-5 last:pb-0"><span className="absolute top-7 bottom-0 left-[13px] w-px bg-line"></span><span className="mono flex size-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-line-strong bg-card text-[11px] text-ink">1</span><div className="pt-0.5"><div className="text-[14px] font-semibold">Design</div><div className="mt-0.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">The creator chooses the launch identity, socials and a mode. Scheduled tokens also commit their plan.</div></div></li><li className="relative flex gap-4 pb-5 last:pb-0"><span className="absolute top-7 bottom-0 left-[13px] w-px bg-line"></span><span className="mono flex size-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-line-strong bg-card text-[11px] text-ink">2</span><div className="pt-0.5"><div className="text-[14px] font-semibold">Pin</div><div className="mt-0.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">The image and generation-zero metadata document are pinned to IPFS.</div></div></li><li className="relative flex gap-4 pb-5 last:pb-0"><span className="absolute top-7 bottom-0 left-[13px] w-px bg-line"></span><span className="mono flex size-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-line-strong bg-card text-[11px] text-ink">3</span><div className="pt-0.5"><div className="text-[14px] font-semibold">Create</div><div className="mt-0.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">One transaction creates the mint, metadata and bonding-curve pool from the launchpad&#x27;s DBC config, with an optional first buy and a <code className="mono rounded border border-line bg-card-2 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[12.5px] text-ink">shift:launch</code> memo. The browser generates the mint keypair; it never leaves the creator&#x27;s device.</div></div></li><li className="relative flex gap-4 pb-5 last:pb-0"><span className="absolute top-7 bottom-0 left-[13px] w-px bg-line"></span><span className="mono flex size-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-line-strong bg-card text-[11px] text-ink">4</span><div className="pt-0.5"><div className="text-[14px] font-semibold">Verify</div><div className="mt-0.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Before broadcasting, the server checks the signed transaction is the one it built and simulates it.</div></div></li><li className="relative flex gap-4 pb-5 last:pb-0"><span className="absolute top-7 bottom-0 left-[13px] w-px bg-line"></span><span className="mono flex size-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-line-strong bg-card text-[11px] text-ink">5</span><div className="pt-0.5"><div className="text-[14px] font-semibold">Live</div><div className="mt-0.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">The token trades on its curve immediately, and its mode takes effect.</div></div></li><li className="relative flex gap-4 pb-5 last:pb-0"><span className="mono flex size-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-line-strong bg-card text-[11px] text-ink">6</span><div className="pt-0.5"><div className="text-[14px] font-semibold">Graduate</div><div className="mt-0.5 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">When the curve fills, liquidity migrates to a Meteora DAMM v2 pool. Shifts continue after graduation.</div></div></li></ol><h2 id="market" className="group mt-16 scroll-mt-24 border-t border-line pt-10 text-[26px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] first:mt-0 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><a href="#market" className="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline gap-3"><span className="mono text-[12px] font-normal text-ink-faint">11</span><span>Market structure</span><span className="mono text-[14px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h2><div className="no-scrollbar mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line"><table className="w-full min-w-[560px] border-collapse text-left text-[13px]"><thead><tr className="border-b border-line bg-card"><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">Parameter</th><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Curve</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Meteora Dynamic Bonding Curve, quoted in SOL</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Supply</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">1,000,000,000, fixed</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Starting market cap</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">≈ 30 SOL</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Graduation</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">≈ 550 SOL market cap (≈ 104 SOL in the curve)</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Trading fee</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">2% on the curve, 2% on the graduated pool</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Graduated liquidity</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Migrated to Meteora DAMM v2 and permanently locked</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="trust" className="group mt-16 scroll-mt-24 border-t border-line pt-10 text-[26px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] first:mt-0 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><a href="#trust" className="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline gap-3"><span className="mono text-[12px] font-normal text-ink-faint">12</span><span>Trust model</span><span className="mono text-[14px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h2><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">STS-1 is explicit about where trust sits. The launchpad holds the update authority for every shiftable token. That is what makes shifts possible without asking holders to sign anything, and it means holders rely on the launchpad to follow this standard.</p><div className="no-scrollbar mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line"><table className="w-full min-w-[560px] border-collapse text-left text-[13px]"><thead><tr className="border-b border-line bg-card"><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">The launchpad can</th><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">The launchpad cannot</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Rewrite a token&#x27;s name, ticker, image and description</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Mint tokens, change supply or decimals</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Pay for and submit shift transactions</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Move, freeze or touch anyone&#x27;s balance</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">Pause shifts for a token (dormancy)</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Change the pool, or move graduated liquidity</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div className="mt-5 rounded-xl border px-4 py-3 border-red/30 bg-red-soft"><div className="mono text-[10.5px] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-red">Caution</div><div className="mt-1 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">A shiftable token&#x27;s name and image are, by design, not permanent. Judge a shiftable token by its mint address, its history and its market, not by the identity it wears today.</div></div><h2 id="integrate" className="group mt-16 scroll-mt-24 border-t border-line pt-10 text-[26px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] first:mt-0 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><a href="#integrate" className="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline gap-3"><span className="mono text-[12px] font-normal text-ink-faint">13</span><span>Integrating</span><span className="mono text-[14px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h2><h3 id="integrate-detect" className="group mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]"><a href="#integrate-detect" className="cursor-pointer">Detecting STS-1 tokens<span className="mono ml-2 text-[12px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h3><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">A token is STS-1 if its metadata account is shiftable, its update authority is the launchpad&#x27;s key, and its creation transaction carries the <code className="mono rounded border border-line bg-card-2 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[12.5px] text-ink">shift:launch</code> memo. Its metadata document lists <code className="mono rounded border border-line bg-card-2 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[12.5px] text-ink">Shifts</code> and <code className="mono rounded border border-line bg-card-2 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[12.5px] text-ink">Mode</code>attributes.</p><h3 id="integrate-index" className="group mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]"><a href="#integrate-index" className="cursor-pointer">Indexing shifts<span className="mono ml-2 text-[12px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h3><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">Wallets and explorers <span className="mono text-[12px] font-semibold tracking-[0.06em] text-ink">SHOULD</span> re-read a token&#x27;s metadata account when they see a transaction from its update authority carrying a <code className="mono rounded border border-line bg-card-2 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[12.5px] text-ink">shift:shift:&lt;n&gt;</code> memo, and <span className="mono text-[12px] font-semibold tracking-[0.06em] text-ink">SHOULD NOT</span> cache an STS-1 token&#x27;s identity indefinitely. The memo&#x27;s generation lets an indexer detect and order rewrites without diffing accounts.</p><h3 id="integrate-api" className="group mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]"><a href="#integrate-api" className="cursor-pointer">HTTP API<span className="mono ml-2 text-[12px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h3><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">Everything the site shows is available as JSON from <code className="mono rounded border border-line bg-card-2 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[12.5px] text-ink">shift-spl.com</code>.</p><div className="no-scrollbar mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line"><table className="w-full min-w-[560px] border-collapse text-left text-[13px]"><thead><tr className="border-b border-line bg-card"><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">Method</th><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">Path</th><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">Returns</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink"><span className="mono text-[12px]">GET</span></td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft"><span className="mono text-[12px] text-ink">/api/specimens</span></td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Live tokens, newest first. ?creator=&lt;wallet&gt; filters, ?limit= up to 200.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink"><span className="mono text-[12px]">GET</span></td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft"><span className="mono text-[12px] text-ink">/api/specimens/:mint</span></td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">One token: identity, market data, schedule (future entries hidden), shift history, recent trades.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink"><span className="mono text-[12px]">GET</span></td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft"><span className="mono text-[12px] text-ink">/api/specimens/:mint/candles</span></td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">USD candles for the chart. ?tf=1m | 15m | 1H | 4H | 1D.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink"><span className="mono text-[12px]">POST</span></td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft"><span className="mono text-[12px] text-ink">/api/specimens/:mint/shift</span></td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Creator shift. Body: name, symbol, image, description, issued, signature.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink"><span className="mono text-[12px]">POST</span></td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft"><span className="mono text-[12px] text-ink">/api/specimens/:mint/mode</span></td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Switch between manual and auto. Body: mode, issued, signature.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink"><span className="mono text-[12px]">GET</span></td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft"><span className="mono text-[12px] text-ink">/api/shifts</span></td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Every shift across the platform, newest first.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink"><span className="mono text-[12px]">GET</span></td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft"><span className="mono text-[12px] text-ink">/api/trending</span></td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">The coins auto-mode tokens will mirror next.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink"><span className="mono text-[12px]">GET</span></td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft"><span className="mono text-[12px] text-ink">/api/config</span></td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Launchpad facts: DBC config, quote mint, keeper interval, SOL price.</td></tr><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink"><span className="mono text-[12px]">GET</span></td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft"><span className="mono text-[12px] text-ink">/api/keeper</span></td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Run one keeper pass (scheduled; ?auto=1 also trending). Bearer KEEPER_SECRET when set.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="faq" className="group mt-16 scroll-mt-24 border-t border-line pt-10 text-[26px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] first:mt-0 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><a href="#faq" className="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline gap-3"><span className="mono text-[12px] font-normal text-ink-faint">14</span><span>FAQ</span><span className="mono text-[14px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h2><div className="mt-4 space-y-2"><details className="card group p-4 [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"><summary className="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-[14px] font-semibold">Do I need to do anything when a token I hold shifts?<span className="text-[18px] text-ink-faint transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p className="mt-2 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">No. Same token, same balance, same address. Your wallet shows the new name and image the next time it refreshes the token.</p></details><details className="card group p-4 [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"><summary className="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-[14px] font-semibold">Can a creator rug through a shift?<span className="text-[18px] text-ink-faint transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p className="mt-2 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">A shift can only change how the token is presented. It cannot mint, move balances or touch liquidity; those are outside what the update authority controls.</p></details><details className="card group p-4 [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"><summary className="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-[14px] font-semibold">Why can&#x27;t I edit a scheduled token&#x27;s plan?<span className="text-[18px] text-ink-faint transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p className="mt-2 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Because the plan is a promise to holders. A schedule that could be rewritten would be manual mode with extra steps.</p></details><details className="card group p-4 [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"><summary className="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-[14px] font-semibold">Will a shifted token confuse charts and screeners?<span className="text-[18px] text-ink-faint transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p className="mt-2 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Charts follow the mint address, so price history is continuous across every identity.</p></details><details className="card group p-4 [&amp;_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"><summary className="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-[14px] font-semibold">What happens to auto tokens if trending data is down?<span className="text-[18px] text-ink-faint transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p className="mt-2 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">That round is skipped and they keep their current identity until the next one.</p></details></div><h2 id="versions" className="group mt-16 scroll-mt-24 border-t border-line pt-10 text-[26px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] first:mt-0 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><a href="#versions" className="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline gap-3"><span className="mono text-[12px] font-normal text-ink-faint">15</span><span>Versioning</span><span className="mono text-[14px] text-ink-faint opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100">#</span></a></h2><div className="no-scrollbar mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line"><table className="w-full min-w-[560px] border-collapse text-left text-[13px]"><thead><tr className="border-b border-line bg-card"><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">Revision</th><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">Date</th><th className="mono px-3 py-2 text-[10.5px] font-normal tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-faint uppercase">Changes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr className="border-b border-line align-top last:border-b-0"><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink">STS-1</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">2026-10-20</td><td className="px-3 py-2.5 text-ink-soft">Initial standard: manual, scheduled and auto modes; signed creator requests; keeper; leases; dormancy.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p className="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-soft">Future revisions will be additive. A token launched under one revision keeps that revision&#x27;s guarantees for life.</p><div className="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-2"><a className="btn btn-ink" href="/lab">Launch a token</a><a href="https://x.com/shiftspl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" className="btn">Follow @shiftspl</a></div></article>  );
}
